Veran
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/signal_array]

# --- COLOR ---
# [] brass throat-button stamped with the Kesharat mark, edge worn from constant brushing
# [] tea cup chipped at the rim, the crack running from lip to base
# [] foreman's belt buckle tarnished dark at the hinge, polished smooth on the edge
# [] sun-creased neck still damp at the back, sweat lines tracking through the dust
# [] neck cloth folded crisp, the crease still showing from this morning's press
# [] boots dry at the toe, leather cracked but not scuffed, heels worn even
# [] hatband dust-pale at the inside fold, no sign of sweat or oil
# [] hand resting on the torque bar, thumb tracing the groove where the grip was worn
# [] tea kettle perched on a stone, its spout stained black from repeated pouring
# [] fingers of the left hand flexing once, then settling, habitual, not tense
# [] collar buttoned to the throat, the seam still sharp after hours in the sun
# [] tea steam rising in a thin thread, then breaking apart before it clears the lip
# --- end ---

FIXME(mundane): Veran is across from you at the rest circle, finishing his tea. He waits for what you might say.

choices:

* Press him on the geometry = Ask him to walk you through the route again [requires !tag signal_array.pressed_veran]
    FIXME(dread): You ask him to walk you through it again. He has a second explanation ready. It does not close either. He seems mildly puzzled that you are asking, but not concerned, and not defensive. He returns to the route description with the same confidence as before.
    +add_tag signal_array.pressed_veran
    +open "Veran"

* Step back to the circle = Let the conversation end
    FIXME(mundane): You let the talk turn. Veran returns to the work. The previous site was good. The cable team there was tight. The next site is two days east. He is proud of the crew. He is proud of the work.
    +add_tag signal_array.met_veran
    +open "The Rest Interval"
